            "evidence": [
              "engine/settings/recognize.go moves entryContainsBinary logic unchanged as entryMentions/commandMentions (bare or shell-quoted substring over hooks[].command); no new input parsing, no shell execution, no file or network access, so no injection or data exposure surface is introduced.",
              "engine/settings/codexhooks/document.go owns() now calls CommandOwnedBy on the handler's command string; the empty-binary guard remains first, so the empty-path-matches-everything case is still refused before uninstall/filter logic that could remove handlers.",
              "engine/status/status.go tightens status checks from the substring gentle-ai-overlay to the full installed path plus family token. This is a stricter, requested (per odd/tasks/consolidation-phase9.md) read-only diagnostic change; it reduces false OK verdicts for another copy of the binary and does not weaken any guard. Note the status checks are not authorization enforcement; the matching remains substring-based, which is pre-existing behavior.",
              "No secrets, dependency changes, or lockfiles are in the candidate. The review-receipt JSON files and task doc are recorded state with no runtime effect; golden and test changes only pin the new notes."
