            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R4-001",
                "lens": "resilience",
                "location": "engine/settings/recognize.go:11-13",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "CommandOwnedBy does not guard an empty binary path (acknowledged in its comment). The status checks now pass the computed binaryPath as hookCommand; if that path were ever empty, every hook command would match on the binary side and status would report OK on the token alone. Codex owns guards this, but the status path does not. Reaching it needs an empty binary path, which the status flow does not normally produce, so this is a hardening note rather than a regression.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/settings/recognize.go:11-13",
                  "engine/status/status.go:200-207"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 16 manifest paths. The change consolidates the hook recognizers into recognize.go and moves five status checks from the bare name substring to the installed path plus the family token, so a hook of another copy of the binary no longer reads as OK.",
              "entryMentions in engine/settings/recognize.go is the removed entryContainsBinary with the same logic, so the family, query and status callers keep their prior behavior. HasLabdrianOwnedHook now goes through hookFamily.carries, which performs the same two-word check as before.",
              "The stricter status match is the owner-requested change recorded in odd/tasks/consolidation-phase9.md. It makes status fail or warn more often on entries that name a different binary path, which is the intended verdict change, and the goldens and unit tests pin the new notes and the new base-hooks-without-minimalism case.",
              "No candidate-caused failure-handling, retry, latency or load defect was found. The work is pure string matching over an already-loaded settings document, with no I/O or loops added.",
              "The receipt JSON files and the task document are recorded review state and notes, with no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
