            "evidence": [
              "engine/settings/recognize.go moves entryContainsBinary unchanged as entryMentions. It still matches the word bare or shell-quoted over each inner hooks[].command, and a non-map entry or missing hooks still gives false. The callers in family.go, query.go and status.go keep their behavior.",
              "engine/settings/status.go: HasLabdrianOwnedHook now delegates to hookFamily.carries, which is the same two-word check as the closure it replaces. engine/settings/codexhooks/document.go: owns now calls CommandOwnedBy on the handler's command string. The empty-binary guard still runs first, and a missing command string gives an empty command, which is false.",
              "engine/status/status.go: the five hook checks now match the installed binary path plus the family token, and their notes name both through the referencing helper. This narrows the match from the bare binary name, which the C6b entry in odd/tasks/consolidation-phase9.md records as an owner-requested change to status output and verdicts, so it is not a regression.",
              "engine/status/status_test.go covers the changed behavior. It tests a bare and a shell-quoted path, the binary name under another path, the binary without the family word, and every hook under another home. engine/cmd/status_golden_test.go adds a golden case for base hooks without the minimalism word, and the goldens are consistent with it.",
              "engine/settings/recognize_test.go covers bare, quoted (with an apostrophe), identity-only, binary-only and empty-command cases for CommandOwnedBy. It also checks that each family's written entries are recognized for their own binary and not for another.",
              "I could not see MissingShaperClearanceGuardParts, HasHookContaining or HasMatchedHookContaining, which are outside this candidate. I judged their path matching from the tests and goldens only. The review-state receipt files and the task document have no runtime effect. I found no candidate-caused reliability defect."
            ]
